    why: ["Correct. Hariot describes a strange new sickness that followed the English from town to town; Old World diseases such as smallpox and measles killed huge numbers of Native people who had never been exposed to them.",
      "Hariot says the people died \"without weapons\" and that the English left the towns \"vnpunished.\"",
      "Hariot describes a disease no one could cure, not hunger.",
      "The deaths came after English visits, and Hariot ties them to sickness, not war."],
